  "measures": [],
  "notes": "A mode-locked fibre laser (500 fs sech² pulses at 1560 nm, 80 MHz) split into two 17.4 m spools. Top: standard single-mode fibre, whose dispersion is anomalous at 1560 nm, at just the peak power (about 218 W) where self-phase modulation and dispersion balance: a fundamental soliton, which arrives as short as it left with its spectrum unchanged, five dispersion lengths on. Bottom: a fibre with normal dispersion (D = −20 ps/(nm km)) at the same power: self-phase modulation broadens the spectrum and dispersion stretches the chirped pulse, to several picoseconds. Each screen’s Pulse tab shows the pulse and its spectrum; select a fibre for its B-integral. Halve the laser’s power and the soliton no longer holds; double it and it narrows and breathes (a higher-order soliton).",
  "ui": {
    "sel": "sA",
    "pins": [],
    "views": {
      "sA": {
        "screenTab": "pulse"
      }
    }
  }
